DECODING LOG  |  wav2vec2 + LoRA (the model from train.log)  |  greedy vs beam vs beam + KenLM  |  FINISHED
====================================================================================================

MODEL
  speech model     outputs/wav2vec2-lora-kaa/final_model  (wav2vec2-xls-r-300m + LoRA, trained in train.log)
  language model   KenLM 4-gram word model: outputs/wav2vec2-lora-kaa/lm/kaa_4gram.arpa
                   built from the 17,685 training transcripts (STT train + HF train)
  code             src/decode.py

DECODERS
  greedy   take the most likely letter at each step, no language model
  beam     beam search (width 100), no language model
  kenlm    beam search (width 100) + the KenLM language model

DATA
  STT validation   1,950 clips, 9.28 h  (its first 500 clips are also used to tune alpha/beta)
  STT test         1,950 clips, 9.18 h
  HF test          523 clips, 0.71 h
  folders          STT = data/final/stt, HF = data/final/hf (Mendeley is not used)

RUN
  machine    server (NVIDIA GB10 GPU), 2026-10-14, finished 18:23
  saved to   outputs/wav2vec2-lora-kaa/results/  (decoder_results.json, decoded_<set>.csv)

STEP 1: TUNE THE LANGUAGE MODEL  (kenlm decoder, first 500 STT validation clips, WER)
              beta 0.0   beta 1.0   beta 2.0
  alpha 0.3     20.38%     20.96%     21.88%
  alpha 0.5     19.63%     19.73%     20.05%
  alpha 0.7     20.17%     19.78%     19.61%   <- best: alpha 0.7, beta 2.0
  alpha 1.0     24.47%     22.54%     21.51%
  alpha = how much the language model counts, beta = bonus for each word

STEP 2: RESULTS  (WER / CER, kenlm uses alpha 0.7 and beta 2.0)
  data             clips           greedy             beam            kenlm
  STT validation   1,950   38.35% / 8.71%   37.56% / 8.51%   18.97% / 5.93%
